# Cloudflare Pages redirects — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# PDFs used to be content-hashed like the CSS and JS (8 hex characters under the old Gulp build,
# 10 under scripts/cache-bust.js), so every PDF URL search engines and other sites picked up had
# a hash in it, and that URL 404'd as soon as the hash changed. PDFs are now published at their
# plain filenames, and these send every hashed URL that was ever live to the stable one.
#
# Exact paths rather than a splat: `/pdfs/wedding-price-list-2025.*` would also match the stable
# `/pdfs/wedding-price-list-2025.pdf` and redirect it to itself. Each PDF has only ever had one
# version in git, so this list is complete; nothing new gets hashed, so it won't grow.

